+## Cleanup phase
+
+The main orchestrator performs it inline — no dispatch, no review, no user gate — after impl-review DoD (`standard`) or design-promote (`lite`); it always returns `NEXT: retro`. Frozen `state.json.cleanup` `false` → no-op ("No-op phase rule").
+
+**Reach**: the sprint diff over `git.base_branch` plus code the sprint's work made superfluous (pre-existing included), removed only on clear evidence — no reference left, debug-only output, a commented-out block, a scratch file, fixture/test data no remaining test reads. Order: debug output, comments, scratch files; then fixtures/test data; then consequential dead code. Kept: stubs and TODOs still needed. Excluded: test files (the test-removal gate, `checkpoints.md` "Gate inventory"), `.asd/sprints/**`, `.asd/project/**` except a resolved stub's `stubs.md` row, `.asd/tmp/**`, `.claude/agent-memory/**`, generated views, persistent `docs/**`, `test-plan.md`, `manual-steps.md`, consumer workflow infrastructure; under `self_hosting` canon prose only as residue of a removal, never a documentation-economy edit.
+
+**Write points** (re-entry reads them in order):
+1. Entry: commit a dirty `timing.jsonl` alone, then the orchestrator's own bookkeeping; any other dirty path is `FAILED` naming it, never committed or discarded. Before the first removal append `- YYYY-MM-DD — cleanup checkpoint <sha>` to `decisions-log.md`.
+2. Each removal commits over its named paths per `git-strategy.md` "Commit before review", subject `chore(cleanup): <what>`, no `ASD-Task` trailer; a removed TODO marker deletes its `stubs.md` row in the same commit.
+3. Verification: build (`commands.yaml` `build`; under `self_hosting` `sync.js --check` judged by its report items, `--apply` over stale views first), lint inside each commit's one-command form, then the impacted tests ("Impacted test set" — this repo's is the full `node tests/run.js`). A red check is diagnosed: fix only what cleanup's own removals broke, or revert the offending removal to the checkpoint; if reverting every removal leaves it red the cause is not cleanup's → `FAILED` naming it.
+4. Record: append `- YYYY-MM-DD — cleanup: removed <paths/symbols|none>; reverted <ids|none>; verified <build, lint, tests @sha>` (`t_decisions-log.md`) — the run's only record; `test-plan.md` is untouched.
+
+**Re-entry**: no checkpoint line → start; checkpoint line without record line → uncommitted paths are the phase's own and are restored from the checkpoint, committed removals stand, verification re-runs; record line → done.
 
