+- Read `research.md` first and research only the technical delta it leaves (`design-principles.md` §11).
+- Integrate an existing draft, preserving `provenance` + `source` when present, and write the draft in `language.docs`.
+- **Authoring** (`core.md` "Incremental writing"; steps 6, 8, 9): write the template's skeleton to the draft path, then per section draft → write → delta summary in `language.chat` (`language-policy.md` "Write-then-review-accept: chat-language self-sufficiency") → `Lock in` or `Revise this section`; after the last section, one artifact-level `accept`, on which append a decisions-log entry ("`<draft path>` accepted") and a `gate_decisions` entry (`gate: <document> accept`, `decision_actor: user`). Re-entry: a section holding content and no `{{` placeholder is locked in, never re-asked; a draft with every section locked in and no `gate_decisions` entry resumes at the accept.
+- Acceptance criteria are atomic, one assertion each; every story cross-references its ACs and every AC its story, none without a story. A requirement dropped, or two sources in conflict, is a user decision before the draft carries either.
+- `design-md-delta.yaml` holds proposed DESIGN.md token changes, each approved at the step 7 token gate.
 
